<figure id="S5.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.03886v1/figs/pdfs/fig_8.jpg" id="S5.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/194;" width="476" height="194" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Qualitative comparison of Text-to-Video generation results between the standard CogVideoX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> and CogVideoX with our method applied, evaluated on custom rare prompts.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Generalizability Across Various Text-to-Vision Tasks</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RareBench in text-to-video generation.</span>
To verify the effectiveness of our method across diverse tasks, we extended our approach to text-to-video generation using the MM-DiT-based CogVideoX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> and evaluated rare-prompt performance on RareBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> with GPT4o-MT scores <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> and a human study (Table. <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Rare Text Semantics Were Always There in Your Diffusion Transformer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
In most evaluation categories, our method improves performance by over 20<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\%p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>%</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%p</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting its effectiveness in enhancing semantic alignment across diverse visual As illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S5.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 5.1 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Rare Text Semantics Were Always There in Your Diffusion Transformer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, our method enables the baseline model to effectively capture rare concepts from the prompts (<span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</span> “<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathtt{...fox\ playing\ piano...}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>𝚏𝚘𝚡</mi><mi>𝚙𝚕𝚊𝚢𝚒𝚗𝚐</mi><mi>𝚙𝚒𝚊𝚗𝚘</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{...fox\ playing\ piano...}</annotation></semantics></math>”), allowing these concepts to emerge clearly across temporal motion and action at each frame of the generated videos. Additional results and ablation studies for video generation are provided in the §<span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#2E8B57;">F</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.SS2.fig3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:110.4pt;">
<div id="S5.T2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:110.4pt;height:51.9pt;vertical-align:-24.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-22.7pt,10.7pt) scale(0.708432555739077,0.708432555739077) ;">
